Sheets: adding a conditional format to a range copies and registers each distinct cell format once (large workbooks open faster).
ScAttrArray::AddCondFormat copied the cell format of every run of cells in the range, added the conditional
format to the copy and registered it. Registering finds an equal format that is already registered, so equal
inputs always end in the same format, but workbooks whose neighbouring cells have different formats have one
run per cell: loading a synthetic 48 MB workbook (300 000 rows, 4000 cell formats, five conditional formats over
its columns) spent a third of its import in these copies and registrations (SfxItemSet copies, hash codes and
comparisons). One call now keeps the registered result of each input format and gives it to the next runs with
that format (sc/inc/hstpatternmemo.hxx); the memo holds the input and the result, so neither can be freed and
replaced by another format at the same address during the call. Every cell gets the same format as before.
Test: CppunitTest_sc_ucalc_condformat testAddCondFormatKeepsEachCellFormat.
License: sc/inc/hstpatternmemo.hxx is HST Office code (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); the modified upstream files
keep their license (MPL-2.0).
